This code simulates a clean energy monitoring system using the Raspberry Pi. It uses the `gpiozero` library to simulate a light sensor connected to GPIO17 and a temperature sensor connected to GPIO4. The `picamera2` library is not used in this example, but it can be used to capture images of the light sensor. The `adafruit-circuitpython-dht` library is used to read the temperature sensor. The `paho-mqtt` library is used to publish sensor data to an MQTT broker. The system logs sensor data and issues warnings and critical messages when the light level falls below the low light threshold, the temperature exceeds the high temperature threshold, or the Pi's internal temperature exceeds the high Pi temperature threshold. The system shuts down when the Pi's internal temperature exceeds the high Pi temperature threshold. The system also shuts down when the user interrupts the program.

