    exit(0)
```

This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to blink an LED connected to GPIO17 indefinitely with a one-second on and one-second off cycle, printing a message each time the LED turns on and each time it turns off. It also catches a KeyboardInterrupt and any error that occurs during initialization of the GPIO pin or LED object, prints an appropriate error message before exiting, and ensures the LED is turned off and all resources are released in every exit path. The code uses the gpiozero, picamera2, adafruit-circuitpython-mcp3008, and paho-mqtt v2 libraries.

